attempts.raw:
@start **The window opens on a single spine column.** Column 0, `tmaR`, is carried by 100% of chromosomes, all persistent, in a region of plasticity in 2% of calls {S1}. The model names 98% of them, at 0.11 bits {S1, M}.

@variable **The rest of the window is fork and variable columns**, 1 to 79, carried by 6 to 90%, in a region of plasticity in 26 to 75% of calls {S2}. A branch of 18 shell families runs through columns 1 to 18 in 16%, [[propanediol utilization microcompartments]] {S2.b1, Q}. The `cobU` to `cobT` genes, columns 23 to 25, are [[adenosylcobinamide biosynthesis]] {S2.c23-25, Q}.

@model **The model names more genes on the spine column than on the fork and variable ones**, 98% against 81%, and hesitates less there, 0.11 against 0.93 bits {M}. Its most hesitant column, 1, is a fork column, at 2.64 bits {H}.

@end **The window ends on the `fli` genes**, columns 57 to 70, [[flagellar assembly]] {S2.c57-70, Q}. The last column is `ftnA`, in 9% of chromosomes {E}.

@whole **Across the window it names 81% of genes**, 0.92 bits on average, perplexity 2.7 families {G}. Inside a region of plasticity it hesitates more than outside, 1.49 against 0.41 bits, and names fewer genes, 70% against 92% {C}.

